     "page": 1,
     "text": "Woodard LLC Clinic\nRe: Gwendolyn Orozco (DOB 10/22/1965)\n\nAugust 12, 2025: Today I saw Gwendolyn Orozco for a follow-up on her Breast cancer, stage II. Her blood pressure was 141/89 and her weight was 156 pounds. Gwendolyn is doing well, with no signs of recurrence and maintaining her quality of life. She is currently on letrozole mg to manage her condition.\n\nNovember 17, 2024: Gwendolyn was seen today for her routine follow-up regarding Breast cancer, stage II. Her blood pressure at this visit was 154/95 and her weight was 159 pounds. She has been stable since her treatment, which began approximately 2.3 years ago. She continues to be on letrozole 2.5 mg as part of her ongoing treatment regimen.\n\nFebruary 23, 2024: Gwendolyn visited today with a complaint of a rash. Her blood pressure was 153/93 her weight was 155 pounds. She also reported having Breast cancer, stage II, which she has been managing since her treatment about 2.3 years ago. We will monitor the and continue her treatment with letrozole 2.5 mg.\n\nMay 30, 2023: Gwendolyn came in today for her annual flu shot. Her blood pressure was 149/84 and her weight was 168 pounds. She mentioned her ongoing management of Breast cancer, stage II, which she has been under control since her treatment approximately 2.3 years ago. Letrozole 2.5 mg is part of her continued therapy.\n\nSeptember 04, 2022: was seen today for a follow-up regarding her Breast cancer, stage II. At the time, her blood pressure was 139/88 and her weight was 164 pounds. She has been in a stable condition since her treatment, which began about 2.3 years prior. She remains on letrozole 2.5 mg to manage her cancer.\n\nDecember 09, 2021: Gwendolyn visited today for a check-up regarding her Breast cancer, stage II. Her blood pressure was 154/91 and her weight was 162 pounds. She is doing well with her condition managed since her treatment approximately 2.3 years ago. She continues her treatment with letrozole 2.5 mg.\n\nAdditionally, Gwendolyn engages in regular physical activity, running 3-4 times a week. She has a history of tobacco use, having smoked one cigarette per day until she quit in September 2022. She minimizes the impact of this habit in her medical history. Gwendolyn also reports consuming approximately three alcoholic drinks per week. Her family history includes her mother who had hypertension, developing the condition at age 77 and passing away at 91.\n"
